Z||000003||Justin||07-26-2001||02:54 PM||||You had an Eagle Talon?  I was looking at a 1993 Talon DL with a 4 cyl and a 5 speed, and I was wandering how fast they were.  What model did you have?  How would the car I was looking at compare to a V6 Fiero, or even a 4 cyl Fiero?  Oh yeah and it's not the Turbo or AWD model, just the base DL model.  <P>------------------<BR>If at first you don't succeed, pretend you were never trying in the first place.<P>visit <A HREF="http://www.twinkiesproject.com" TARGET=_blank>www.twinkiesproject.com</A>  for information on the chemical properties, reactions, gravitational resonse, and density issues of a Twinkie.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wannabe||07-26-2001||08:30 PM||||Let's try this then  <A HREF="http://www.blacksphotocentre.com/viewphoto.asp?id=F2CA6783-AC0B-4DFC-95DD-2746019B882A&iImgPos=6" TARGET=_blank>http://www.blacksphotocentre.com/viewphoto.asp?id=F2CA6783-AC0B-4DFC-95DD-2746 019B882A&iImgPos=6</A> <P>The Fiero and the Talon are very different animals. I believe the DL is the 1.8L version....unless you need a practical, economical car that can haul some stuff around, the Fiero is much more desireable, all around. I had the TSI AWD with some very small mods. The TSI AWD or FWD are very fast cars with huge potential for more. The handling is excellent on the street, but leaves something to be desired for the track. I'm enjoying the Formula MUCH more than the TSI. Personally, i would stay away from the DL, hold out for at least the 2.0L FWD, which is a quick car. The tubo FWD is a real kick in the pants, but not the best handler either.<p>[This message has been edited by Wannabe (edited 07-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||DecadenceR||07-26-2001||08:39 PM||||I had an eclipse, same animal except it wasn't available with AWD.<BR>Anyway, the 1.8 is a pretty junky motor. If you get one, at least get the 2.0L they're pretty damn quick and handle REAL good. Not as tight as a Fiero, but i had no problem with it ever except after my mods I had a problem keeping the front straight at launching.<p>[This message has been edited by DecadenceR (edited 07-26-2001).]||||reg||1
